tops": 0, "is_error": false, "num_turns": 5, "subtype": "success", "api_error_status": null, "result": "The spec is implemented and the check it lists passes: `.venv/bin/python -m pytest -q tests/test_logs_store.py tests/test_openai_responses.py tests/test_migrate.py tests/test_llm_logs.py` gave **266 passed** when I ran it. The implementer also ran the full test suite and reported 998 passed; I didn't re-run that myself.\n\nI read through the full diff and it follows the spec. The changes:\n\n- **`pyproject.toml`**: the dependency is now `condense-json>=1.1`.\n- **`llm/migrations.py`**: new migration `m027_turns_response_json` adds a nullable `turns.response_json` column.\n- **`llm/logs.py`**:\n  - `LogStore.log` now saves the raw provider payload in condensed form. Long strings and JSON chunks that the turn's own messages, tools, schema or the model's dictionary already contain are replaced with short references.\n  - New `LogStore.turn_response_json` rebuilds the full payload from those same rows.\n  - `llm logs` now shows `response_json` instead of always `null`. If one payload can no longer be rebuilt, that row shows `null` and the rest of the listing still works.\n- **`llm/default_plugins/openai_models.py`**: when streaming, the OpenAI Responses plugin now updates the reasoning part with the encrypted content from the final payload. Each turn stores one ciphertext instead of two different ones, and there is still a single reasoning part.\n\nNothing is committed. Ruff isn't installed in `.venv`, so no lint or format check was run.", "ttft_ms": 2562, "type": "result", "duration_ms": 395696, "uuid": "fd7c72fe-a74c-411f-be45-f11e807eafcd", "ttft_stream_ms": 2047, "time_to_request_ms": 411, "first_content_frame_ms": 2047, "queued_turn_count": 0, "result_index": 0}
